    "envious": {
      "word": "ENVIOUS",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Malignant; mischievous; spiteful. [Obs.] Each envious brier his weary legs doth scratch. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Feeling or exhibiting envy; actuated or directed by, or proceeding from, envy; -- said of a person, disposition, feeling, act, etc.; jealously pained by the excellence or good fortune of another; maliciously grudging; -- followed by of, at, and against; as, an envious man, disposition, attack; envious tongues. My soul is envious of mine eye. Keble. Neither be thou envious at the wicked. Prov. xxiv. 19.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Inspiring envy. [Obs. or Poetic] He to him leapt, and that same envious gage Of victor's glory from him snatched away. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Excessively careful; cautious. [Obs.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        }
      ],
